>> title: Hijiki no Nimono
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: japanese, hijiki, seaweed, abura-age, make ahead, side, vegetarian
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: ひじきの煮物, hijiki no nimono, hijiki nimono, ヒジキの煮物, 五目ひじき, gomoku hijiki, simmered hijiki, hijiki seaweed side
>> pairs-with: gohan, chikuzenni
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — three or four days in the fridge and two or three in summer, and the abura-age is what turns first
>> step.1: soak 20 min, drain the water away
>> step.2: fry 3 min
>> step.3: simmer 15 min, until a film is left

Soak @dried hijiki{1%oz}(30 g) in @cold water{4%cups}(950 mL) ~soak{20%min}, until it has swollen to about eight times its dry volume, then drain it and rinse it in fresh water.

Fry @&(~1)soaked hijiki{} with @carrot{1}(in matchsticks) and @abura-age{1%sheet}(doused with boiling water to strip the frying oil, then sliced thin) in @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}(10 mL) in a #saucepan{} ~fry{3%min}, until the hijiki smells toasted rather than of the sea.

Pour @water{1 1/4%cups}(300 mL), @soy sauce{4%Tbs}(60 mL), @sugar{2%Tbs} and @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL) over @&(~1)pan{} and ~simmer{15%min} uncovered, until only a film of liquid is left in the bottom and the carrot has gone soft.
